==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*4 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Ragin' Gory]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*4 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 12~15.33 seconds<sup>360f~460f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns.
**15 [[Li'l Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**8 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 12~15.33 seconds<sup>360f~460f</sup>.
**3 [[Haniwanwan]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
**8 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**1 [[Two Can]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.
**3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Almost every enemy that does not spawn indefinitely can be a huge threat. M. Ost pushes with terrifying ease, Sir Rels rip through everything and Two Can's Waves can be a handful. Even the easily countered Ragin' Gory can become rather threatening at the very beginning. You will want to bring anything helpful for these threats and remove them as quickly as possible, then finish off Nyandam.

With the tight startoff, you would want to use a Rich Cat, and Sniper is great for briefly stalling Nyandam or getting him off your base.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]] - Idi's high movement speed makes timing easier when trying to avoid Nyandam's attacks, while her massive damage to Relics can gravely cripple M. Ost, but requires lots of support in order to get a hit on. Not much different from the [[Mr. Puffington|Puffington]] in [[Aku Reincarnation (Merciless)|Aku Reincarnation]], using Idi to remove M. Ost early in battle makes the rest of the stage that much easier.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]]/[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza]] - Courier is less viable as a general unit, but having Behemoth Slayer and Massive Damage against Reds allows it to counter Ragin' Gory and Two Can with some support. Pizza's massive damage to Darks and Wave talents also makes him more than a match for the same reason. Just make sure not to send them out too often.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus]] - Blocks Two Can and Haniwanwan's waves so your attackers won't get demolished. Will also constantly be pushed into safety by M. Ost, so there's no need to worry about their health.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mohawk Cat]] - Its decent dodge chance against every threat in this stage and low deploy cost makes stalling M. Ost and peons in this stage a lot easier if paired alongside Manic Eraser Cat. Beware, however, that if Brainwashed Mohawk procs dodge too many times on the Two Can, it can and will produce more waves that will decimate your front line if there's no octopus there.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] - Uril has enough range to be just within Nyandam's 1st blindspot, with his slow he can stall the M. Ost as well as the Haniwans, he can also get rid of the Dark and Li'l Doges, having him basically just makes the stage a lot simpler.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Any Uber with a range between 401 and 499 - Any Uber that accomplishes this requirement can make the stage easier due to standing in on the 1st Nyandam blindspot and it also makes the clean up faster.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Hellrider Kenshin]]: With Relic targeting, Kenshin can force everything to stay behind Nyandam using her KB Mini-Waves while also dealing some hefty damage from a safe distance. The Mini-Waves are also strong enough to clear out the Li'l Doges before they get a chance to cause any problems with their dodging. Her [[Cat Combo]], [[Hecks Angels (Combo)|Hecks Angels]], can be used in tandem with [[Spinners (Combo)|Spinners]] to give your Units a much better shot at making it into Nyandam's blind spots without being hit by his Toxic attacks.
*[[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]] - Surprisingly, this Uber is viable in the stage due to being able to stand in Nyandam's second blindspot, while its freeze and weaken is able to help with the support (and Nyandam himself).
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]] - Although she is outranged by Nyandam, the combination of fast and very recurring peons make Kasli being able to have a step stone to snipe Nyandam easily, and for an extra point, her Curse effect is able to disable Nyandam's Toxic and M. Ost's Curse, Slow and Knockback, making their pushing power much weaker while making your units survive longer.
*[[Bunny & Canard (Uber Rare Cat)|Malevolent Mad-Duck]] - Although this unit has Target only against Red and Aku, it boasts extreme stats, can outrange Nyandam/Two Can and is Immune to Toxic, which enables it to land devastating hits and survive for quite a while.
*[[Goddess of Light Sirius (Uber Rare Cat)|Goddess of Light Sirius]] - Safely sits in Nyandam's first blindspot, is toxic immune so you don't have to time her, and deals a nice 9K DPS. Can maybe help with the M. Ost due to her immunities.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] - Can be used to gravely cripple Two Can, similarly to [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], once M. Ost has been eliminated. Does, however, need decent boosting and good timing to avoid peons and the Boss' attacks.
*[[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Phantasmal Nobunaga]] - While Phantasmal Nobunaga does require some setup, his anti-Aku Freeze effect has full uptime compared to his attack cycle (8 seconds > 3.7 seconds), allowing him to easily perma-Freeze Nyandam so other units may focus on killing off his support.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]] - With the survive ability granted by Kasa Jizo's ultra form, he becomes a hybrid of Jiangshi cat and Courier Cat, able to accumulate massive DPS in between Nyandam's attack cycles. He also outranges the support in the stage, being able to deal with M. Ost with minimal extra meatshielding, and incidentally obliterating the occasional Sir Rel, Two Can, and Haniwanwan.
*[[Mighty Morta-Loncha (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Morta-Loncha]] - A near perfect counter against Nyandam due to being able to stay in his first blindspot, having Immunity to Toxic, and being able to Freeze him which makes dealing with his support significantly easier. It can also deal good damage against M. Ost, but the Two Can may pose some trouble due to Morta-Loncha lacking Wave Immunity.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] - He stands comfortably between Nyandam second and third multi-hit being able to one shot all the insignificant peons on the stage (Such as Sir rel, Doge dark and li'l doge) and chipping down Nyandam's health while controlling the field with his insane waves and damage (Requires a lot of meatshield).

==Trivia==
*Infernal Tyrant Climax is the first stage to have a difficulty of Brutal and the first [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] to drop a [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]] at a 100% chance.

